4493:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *  Adds result register to Result FIFO.<BR>\n
4494:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Sometimes, the rate of consumption of results by application software may not match the rate at 
4495:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * results are produced. A Result FIFO thus helps a slow consumer to read out results without loss 
4496:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * When a result register is added to fifo, it is in fact chained to its higher numbered neighbor. 
4497:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Result Register-5 is to be added to FIFO, it gets chained to Result Register-6. Results are writ
4498:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * while the same can be read out of Register-5 leisurely by software.
4499:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * A call to this API would configure the register bit field GxRCR.FEN.
4500:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
4501:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * \par<b>Note:</b><br>
4502:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * The FIFO is always read by the software with the lowest numbered result register.
4503:C:/Workspaces/DAVE-4.3/WS_2016_09_02/XMC1300Stepper9201_V3.2/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * The hardware will write the results from the highest numbered result register.
